The public-URL gate for `web_fetch` now judges IPv4-mapped (`::ffff:a.b.c.d`) and IPv4-compatible (`::a.b.c.d`) literals by their embedded IPv4 (#662 / PR #664). Three other IPv6 forms that also carry an IPv4 address still pass, so the same model-supplied URL can reach loopback or the link-local metadata endpoint through them.

Verified on live main `a074172f60e5667e72ff04246316a0a41552cb46`, `packages/data-source/src/web/native/url-guard.ts`:

- NAT64 well-known prefix `64:ff9b::/96` — the IPv4 address sits in the last two hextets. `ipv6Blocked` only consults `ipv4Blocked` for the mapped/compatible forms (`url-guard.ts:58-68` on main; `:81-97` after #664), so `64:ff9b::...` falls to `return false` (`:68` on main, `:97` after #664).
- 6to4 `2002::/16` — the IPv4 address sits in hextets 2–3, which no branch inspects.
- IPv4-translated `::ffff:0:0:0/96` — 80 zero bits, then `ffff`, then 16 zero bits, then the IPv4 address; it matches neither the mapped test (`hextets[5] === 0xffff`) nor the compatible test (first six hextets zero) that #664 added at `url-guard.ts:95-97`.
- Deprecated site-local `fec0::/10` — the link-local branch tests `fe8`–`feb` only, so `fec0::/10` is reported public.

Current vs expected: `isBlockedAddress("64:ff9b::7f00:1")`, `"2002:7f00:1::"`, `"::ffff:0:7f00:1"` and `"fec0::1"` all return `false`; each must return `true`, and `assertPublicUrl("http://[64:ff9b::7f00:1]/")` and the two siblings must reject with `local and private network URLs are not allowed`. Decoding must stay narrow: `64:ff9b::808:808`, `2002:808:808::` and `::ffff:0:808:808` embed the public `8.8.8.8` and must keep returning `false` — a fix that rejects the whole prefix breaks NAT64 and 6to4 egress.

Suggested red test, in `packages/data-source/src/web/native/providers.test.ts`, next to `web_fetch refuses private and loopback targets`:

```ts
test("web_fetch judges NAT64, 6to4 and IPv4-translated literals by their embedded IPv4", () => {
  for (const address of ["64:ff9b::7f00:1", "2002:7f00:1::", "::ffff:0:7f00:1", "fec0::1"]) {
    assert.equal(isBlockedAddress(address), true, address);
  }
  for (const address of ["64:ff9b::808:808", "2002:808:808::", "::ffff:0:808:808"]) {
    assert.equal(isBlockedAddress(address), false, address);
  }
});
```

Run: `cd packages/data-source && node --import tsx --test src/web/native/providers.test.ts`

Current result on main: 8 of 12 rows red (`false !== true` on the four blocked rows and on the three URL forms; the three public rows pass). Dedupe: open + closed search for `NAT64`, `64:ff9b`, `6to4`, `2002::`, `fec0`, `site-local`, `IPv4-translated` returns only #662/#664, which scope these classes out — no separate issue exists.

Scope note: this is the follow-up the #664 body lists as out of scope. One PR, one class of change: decode the embedded IPv4 for each of these prefixes instead of blocking the prefix.
